\title{Area-under-the-ROC-curve changepoint measure}
\description{
Area under the ROC curve that \code{\link[penaltyLearning:ROChange]{penaltyLearning::ROChange()}} traces by adding one constant to every
predicted penalty \code{log(lambda)}. Each shift selects one model per sequence, and the curve plots the
false positive rate against the true positive rate, totalled over all label regions. The models and
their label errors come from the same pipeline and per-sequence \code{Kmax} as
\link{mlr_measures_changepoint.label_error} (the prediction's recorded cap, else the learner's).
\code{autoplot(prediction, task = task, type = "roc")} draws the curve.

Changepoint ROC curves need not be monotonic: a curve with loops can enclose an area above 1
(Hillman and Hocking 2023), so the range is unbounded.

The measure declares \code{"requires_task"} and \code{"na_score"}: an empty prediction, a non-finite predicted
penalty, or labels with no region that can hold a false positive (or none that can hold a false
negative) score \code{NA}. \code{\link[penaltyLearning:ROChange]{penaltyLearning::ROChange()}} is unweighted, so the measure ignores weights.
}
